    "about": "On a jungle beach east of Tanaris (Tel'Abim, by the map position) the wet sand was broken: a dark band on part of the shore, pieces with straight edges in the middle, none on the rest (2026-10-07, the owner). The wet sand pass drew only on ground under 32 degrees of slope, which keeps bodies and posts dry; the bank here is steeper, and the slope is per terrain triangle, so the band came and went triangle by triangle. Now full up to 60 degrees, none past 72 (NOTES.md, the wet sand on a steep bank). Shot 1 in the normal view, shot 2 in the wet sand alone (Debug View 18), shot 3 in the normal view with the Wet Sand slider at 0 (2026-10-07: the slider is new). Then Old Hillsbrad (the Caverns of Time, map 269), the owner's snapshot over a river, with their settings (2026-10-08): the wet sand on the far bank lay as a contour on the grass, well over the water, with a step at each map cell's edge. A river runs downhill across a chunk, and each map cell took the chunk's highest water level; now the mean of its four points, and the wet pass weighs the cells round a point by how near they are. Shots 4 to 6 as 1 to 3.",
